{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/670407-pretty-cool-film-that-used-bloodlines-as-inspiration","id":670407,"title":"Pretty cool film that used Bloodlines as inspiration.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-18T19:01:09-07:00","id":670407,"title":"Pretty cool film that used Bloodlines as inspiration.","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/139714990\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/filter/overlay?src0=https%3A%2F%2Fi.vimeocdn.com%2Fvideo%2F535704227-f081c5334a68c89f10a48d6bb704c6255200109c3c8ffb8200f7961657a25c48-d_1280x720&amp;src1=https%3A%2F%2Ff.vimeocdn.com%2Fimages_v6%2Fshare%2Fplay_icon_overlay.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/139714990\" target=\"_blank\"> The Intruder </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/139714990\" target=\"_blank\"> https://vimeo.com/139714990 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A demented burglar is accidentally trapped when his victims return home early from a night out. Produced &amp; Directed by Barrett Wolfe -Starring- Sasha&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not sure if this forum was the correct place to post this, but I thought I should share. If any of you remember the quest Imalia gives you in Vampire the Masquerade: Bloodlines, then this short film should entertain you. Tons of easter eggs from the game.<br /> <br /> I thought it was very well done. And...well...it also managed to make me to install Bloodlines. Again.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:34:58-07:00","id":670544,"title":"","content":"Seems as good a place as any. The vtm forum might've just WTFed it. <br /> <br /> Looks really interesting. Despite naysayers, I've always loved Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Currently working my way back through the Slasher (aka dickbag Gangrel) series of missions as a Ventrue. Weirdly, I'd never used a Ventrue before. I feel like a demigod when talking to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T02:47:48-07:00","id":670644,"title":"","content":"I always play as a Ventrue, is lots of fun to do the jedi mind trick in conversations. Saves a lot of Humanity too. Man I'm a fucking saint in that game I always reach Humanity 10 in minutes and never drop. Nosferatu is whole different game and is also awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T03:07:15-07:00","id":670662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/670407-pretty-cool-film-that-used-bloodlines-as-inspiration?p=670644#post670644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always play as a Ventrue, is lots of fun to do the jedi mind trick in conversations. Saves a lot of Humanity too. Man I'm a fucking saint in that game I always reach Humanity 10 in minutes and never drop. Nosferatu is whole different game and is also awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No kidding! I usually use a clan that'd be technically a &quot;low&quot; clan in DA:V or close to it, but this Ventrue run is insanely easy, but only in conversation. I guess it's the Presence/Dominate combination that's built into the game, but it's a totally different experience.<br /> <br /> My last run was as a Gangrel and I did so many side missions just to upgrade myself enough to be a badass. Meanwhile, my Ventrue owns a combat knife and has Dominate 4. He's walking around like fucking Xerxes before Leonidas decided to talk some shit. I have people loving me that have NO earthly reason to trust me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T07:59:21-07:00","id":670952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/670407-pretty-cool-film-that-used-bloodlines-as-inspiration?p=670644#post670644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always play as a Ventrue, is lots of fun to do the jedi mind trick in conversations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ventrue is usually my last pick, but for one reason only: the freaking sewer section. Your disciplines allow you to be every bit as combat-ready as any other clan, but being unable to replenish your blood supply down there (without carrying a blood bank's worth of bags) is a real slog.<br /> <br /> My usual pick is Nosferatu. It's no secret that some of the skills and Disciplines in this game are way more useful than others, and Nosferatu gets bonuses to virtually all the best picks. Plus it's just a cool take on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 09-19-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T22:55:48-07:00","id":673874,"title":"","content":"Cielle, you gave me the itch to play Bloodlines as a nossie. Roar.<br /> Just finished the Ocean House for the millionth time ever, and joined the twins (totally tempted to be a nosferatu dominatrix and go with Jeanette...but the experience points :'( )<br /> <br /> So far, I'm really enjoying not having to go to that shitty apartment all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T23:04:05-07:00","id":673877,"title":"","content":"This wouldn't have derailed if it was in the movies thread. I think we just saw Bloodlines and got excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}